From: thororen <78185467+thororen1234@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 16 Oct 2026 23:09:50 -0400
Subject: fix: allow ANGLE's OpenGL backend on macOS

Chromium stopped allowing ANGLE's OpenGL backend on macOS when it dropped
macOS 12. Allow it again after Metal, so Metal stays the default and Macs
or macOS versions that do not use Metal can select OpenGL with
--use-angle=gl.

This patch is needed for macOS 10.13 through 12 support and is not
suitable for upstreaming.

diff --git a/ui/gl/init/gl_factory_mac.cc b/ui/gl/init/gl_factory_mac.cc
index 3cfe3a42beca96b8a1b522479d6c4f45b2a2811d..212c87dd6d17178199a7f240743a3e8df144e91a 100644
--- a/ui/gl/init/gl_factory_mac.cc
+++ b/ui/gl/init/gl_factory_mac.cc
@@ -26,6 +26,9 @@ namespace init {
 std::vector<GLImplementationParts> GetAllowedGLImplementations() {
   std::vector<GLImplementationParts> impls;
   impls.emplace_back(gl::ANGLEImplementation::kMetal);
+  // Allowed but not the default, for Macs without Metal and macOS versions
+  // that Metal is not used on.
+  impls.emplace_back(gl::ANGLEImplementation::kOpenGL);
   impls.emplace_back(gl::ANGLEImplementation::kSwiftShader);
   return impls;
 }
